WEBVTT


00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:02.320
if you're trying to choose between Japan and South Korea

00:00:02.321 --> 00:00:03.361
let me help you out

00:00:03.362 --> 00:00:06.441
I've been to Japan multiple times and just got back from South Korea

00:00:06.442 --> 00:00:08.481
but your first time start with Japan

00:00:08.482 --> 00:00:09.841
English is more widely spoken

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.821
it's easy to navigate and infrastructure is exceptional

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.020
South Korea can be a little harder to navigate as a first timer

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.600
Google Maps doesn't work well there

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.501
and English isn't as widely spoken outside of tourist areas

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.320
that said South Korea is significantly more affordable

00:00:23.321 --> 00:00:26.601
hotels are cheaper sometimes even better quality for less money

00:00:26.602 --> 00:00:28.601
Japan feels more traditional and cultural

00:00:28.602 --> 00:00:29.961
while South Korea feels modern

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:31.821
fast paced and incredibly stylish

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.060
personally I prefer South Korea's architecture

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:35.760
both countries are extremely safe

00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:37.841
so safety won't really be a factor either way

00:00:37.842 --> 00:00:39.841
but if you can only choose one for your first trip

00:00:39.842 --> 00:00:42.161
start with Japan then go back for South Korea

00:00:42.162 --> 00:00:43.721
you probably want to do both anyway

00:00:43.722 --> 00:00:45.282
so which one are you choosing
